The files in this directory are third-party software, not part of the
lmepisowifi project's own AGPLv3 code:

  sch_fq_codel.ko    Fair Queue CoDel packet scheduler (Linux kernel net/sched)
  sch_cake.ko        CAKE packet scheduler (net/sched/sch_cake.c)
  tc                 iproute2 `tc` traffic-control utility, with CAKE support

Each retains its original license. This NOTICE stands in for a source-file
header (the artifacts are compiled and cannot carry one). Being shipped in this
repository, or in the release tarballs next to the AGPLv3 scripts that use
them, does not relicense them: they are separate works. The two .ko files are
loaded into the kernel on demand by lmehspt.sh; `tc` is a standalone program
that lmehspt.sh runs only when the firmware's own tc cannot create a CAKE qdisc.
No AGPLv3 code is compiled into, or linked against, any of them.

Build
-----
  The kernel modules are built for the Realtek RTL9607C vendor kernel: Linux
  4.4.140, SMP, mod_unload, MIPS32r2, 32-bit, big-endian (see `vermagic` in
  each .ko).

  `tc` is a MIPS32r2 big-endian, dynamically linked (glibc) executable built
  with the Realtek MSDK-4.8.5p1 toolchain (GCC 4.8.5; see its ELF .comment).
  `sch/tc -V` prints the iproute2 version it was built from.


